 "source_passage": "Data-science / analytics / AI firm handling extremely sensitive third-party data (de-identified CBA banking transactions via CommBank iQ, ~A$130bn Iress wealth data, Woolworths loyalty data, health/genomics data). High-data-sensitivity sector and a high-value-target profile, but NO Quantium-specific incident was found. Exposure comes from its parent/sibling (Woolworths MyDeal breach) and the concentration of partner data it holds. The aggregation risk and downstream blast radius (banking, retail, health) make it a strong cyber-cover candidate despite the absence of an own incident. No confirmed Quantium-specific breach found in public sources/OAIC NDB publications as of Jun 2026 (treat as 'no incident found', not a clean bill of health) Parent/sibling exposure: Woolworths' MyDeal breach (~2.2M customers, 2022) reflects the group's wider attack surface Concentration/data-sensitivity risk: custodian of CBA transaction data, Iress wealth data, Woolworths customer data, health/genomics data — outsized downstream impact if breached (inherent-risk indicator, not an incident) Parent/majority owner: Woolworths Group (~75% in 2021 for A$223m; now ~80.4%); combined analytics entity 'wiq' JV partners/customers: Commonwealth Bank (CommBank iQ), Telstra (Quantium Telstra JV) Partner/customer: Iress (FundsFlow data product) Former co-parent link: Endeavour Group (demerged from Woolworths 2021; shared-services link) Tech partner: Google Cloud (Gemini Enterprise practice); vendors Cisco/Cohesity International clients: Walmart/ASDA Auditor via parent: Deloitte (no separate statutory auditor for Quantium confirmed) Competitors: Accenture, Deloitte, Fractal, EXL, Tredence, PwC (competitive overlap, not commercial ties)",
